&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Radar ML team builds the machine learning systems that power Stripe’s Radar fraud and abuse product suite. Our models make real-time decisions across a significant share of internet commerce - helping businesses stop fraud, increase authorization, and grow safely. By turning economy-scale datasets into compelling ML products, the team directly improves customer outcomes and drives meaningful revenue for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is growing, and expanding into multiple new areas. We are building abuse protections across the full customer life-cycle, adaptive and customizable fraud systems for enterprises, and risk intelligence for 50+ global payment methods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own ML problems from conception to production: analyzing new fraud and abuse patterns, exploring large-scale datasets, experimenting with model architectures, designing evaluations, deploying models, and monitoring performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work may include developing transformer architectures for payment data, building graph-powered intelligence across consumers, leveraging LLMs to detect emerging attacks, or rapidly prototyping new protections with frontier AI labs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have opportunities to ship 0→1 products, and to improve mission-critical ML models operating at Stripe scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, train, evaluate, and deploy models that detect fraud and abuse across Stripe’s global network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate emerging fraud and abuse patterns, identify where ML can help, and rapidly develop effective solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design features, datasets, evaluation methods, and experiments for noisy, delayed, and adversarial environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve model architectures, training methods, and production systems to increase model quality, coverage, and adaptability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor production behavior and improve models as data, customer needs, and attack patterns change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance model quality with legitimate-user impact, latency, reliability, and operational complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, product, data science, risk experts, and leading Stripe users to turn modeling improvements into differentiated Radar products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to reusable tools and AI-assisted workflows that help the team develop and operate ML systems more effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a fast, pragmatic problem solver with deep ML expertise and a bias toward action. You are excited to work at the frontier of payments and AI - turning advances in machine learning into production systems that address new forms of fraud and abuse. You’ve built ML models and shepherded them to production, landing impact for users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience developing, evaluating, and deploying machine learning models in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundations in machine learning, data analysis, statistics, model evaluation, and experiment design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming and software-engineering skills, with experience writing tested, maintainable code for production ML applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating production ML systems, including one or more of large-scale data and feature pipelines, distributed model training, low-latency inference, model deployment, or production monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to investigate ambiguous problems, reason from data, and choose pragmatic technical approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate technical ideas and results clearly and collaborate effectively across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning an ML problem across the full lifecycle, from problem framing and data exploration through deployment, monitoring, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or productionizing modern deep learning, graph-learning, or LLM-based approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and optimizing real-time, low-latency ML systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying ML to fraud detection, integrity, trust and safety, identity, cybersecurity, or another adversarial domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience rapidly building 0→1 products, working directly with customers, or operating effectively in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active interest in the latest ML developments, and how they can be leveraged to solve business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable computer systems that manage a large volume of information and use them to fulfill business goals for the company and its partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve backend scalability and performance by integrating lightweight backend framework, overhauling APIs and optimizing database systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build tools that ingest and process signals from various sources to make them more accessible for the company’s partner teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement logging and data visualization system for backend APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and resolve software issues reported from production, automated testing, QA testing and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement scalable and reliable automated testing suites to reduce manual Quality Assurance tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams and streamlined software development and deployment processes with Continuous Integration (CI) and Continuous Delivery (CD) pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Master&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field, plus six (6) years of software development experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have four (4) years of experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building software solutions in Java, C++, Python, or Ruby;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building and maintaining scalable systems;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translating business needs into software requirements and designs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debugging production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed systems; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implementation of scalable high-performance RESTful microservices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $206,086 - $285,600/yr&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions / sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;50% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends. &lt;strong&gt;WA58&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;#LI-DNI &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the &lt;strong&gt;team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Developer &amp;amp; End-user Experience Platform (DEEP) organization empowers all of Stripe&#39;s products with a shared product platform that helps with rapidly delivering high-quality, cross-product experiences across our UI and API surfaces. It focuses on providing a consistent and scalable developer experience that any developer (both internal and external) can leverage to accelerate a merchant&#39;s ability to create value using Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team matching — exact team matching for one of the subteams will begin during final stages. Please note we may also consider you for different orgs based on your experience, location, etc. More information on our team matching process can be found &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zvJkO2c7GzukHG-_oqc5wbOLajpuh5FjbmZPcZPU1o0/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for Backend Engineers who want to make an impact on managing money at a global scale with a passion for building ergonomic APIs. You&#39;ll play a key role in extending our balance management platform and in building out a new funds accessibility platform that enterprises and SMBs use. Our team collaborates with many cross-functional teams—from Infrastructure to Product—at Stripe to deliver innovative solutions that address evolving user needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope, design, build, and maintain APIs, services, and large-scale systems that reliably and efficiently handle billions of money movement requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug and solve critical production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers to help them grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across the company to build new features at large-scale, while improving internal engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively in a distributed and hybrid team, maintaining open communication and strong connections with colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–12+ years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships or co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language (we understand new languages can be learned on the job, so our interview process is language-agnostic)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work across workstreams within your team and contribute to your peers&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive with a high level of autonomy and responsibility, with an entrepreneurial mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in working as a generalist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale financial tracking systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding and practical knowledge in cloud-based services (e.g., gRPC, GraphQL, Docker and Kubernetes, cloud services such as AWS, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supportability Decisions is a Dublin-based engineering team within Supportability Engineering, part of Risk Engineering. We own the “how a business sells” side of Supportability: determining whether a user’s declared business, web presence, account configuration, and observed transaction behaviour align with Stripe’s standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our core domain includes transaction-laundering detection and decisioning, web-presence and URL-policy controls, and low-quality e-commerce detection. We consume the signals and evaluations that support decisions in these spaces and convert them into evidence-based and auditable determinations that can be shared with the rest of the Supportability platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pitch is: join a high-ownership team solving some of Stripe’s hardest risk problems. We build technology that helps Stripe distinguish legitimate businesses from bad actors at scale, combining sophisticated engineering, AI-assisted investigation, and meaningful real-world impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a meaningful part of a risk-decisioning problem from investigation and design through implementation, rollout, measurement, and iteration. You will help build both the domain capabilities and the modern agentic infrastructure required to make Supportability decisions consistent, stateful, explainable, and appropriate to the business, product, and moment in time. Depending on team priorities and the candidate’s experience, this may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building the Supportability Decision Layer: a durable service and API through which automated systems, agents, and human reviewers can request, produce, retrieve, and understand canonical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing the infrastructure that enables agentic investigations to synthesize policy, business identity and history, product context, risk appetite, and multiple assessment signals into explainable, confidence-calibrated decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the transaction-laundering agent’s policy grounding, evidence quality, risk tiering, precision and recall, and use of behavioural, dispute, and other relevant signals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing durable decision state and history, including traceability from supporting evidence through reasoning and applied consequence, and validity and refresh policies that prevent stale outcomes from persisting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building governed, reusable configuration and integration patterns that adapt decision capabilities across products, partners, countries, and permitted risk appetites without creating bespoke systems for each use case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building reliable backend workflows on shared Supportability and Risk Platform infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making complex risk decisions explainable to reviewers and affected users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using data and feedback from outcomes, appeals, and corrections to improve decision quality while balancing the identification of bad actors against avoiding unnecessary harm to legitimate businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modernising URL enforcement, including when and how URL checks run, reducing unnecessary review volume and user friction, and supporting migration away from legacy systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expanding shared SAE/SPO decisioning foundations, including due-diligence support and product-scoped remediation and appeal capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the Process Orchestration Framework and moving workflow code into more maintainable platform packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to future work in automated LPM URL screening, low-quality e-commerce detection, wider web intelligence, and active test charges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 - 7 years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships or co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work effectively across the stack from top to bottom, comfortably navigating codebases with different languages and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re equally comfortable shipping user-facing experiences as you are writing custom queries to analyze experiment results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language (we understand new languages can be learned on the job, so our interview process is language-agnostic)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills, with the ability to work across workstreams within your team and contribute to your peers&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy and responsibility, and think of yourself as entrepreneurial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in working as a generalist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high-growth teams similar to Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building financial systems or tools for financial experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
